The query loads tracked entities, because the caller will modify and save them. I don't use `AsNoTracking()`, and I don't project, since projection would give back untracked values rather than entities. The query uses `AsSplitQuery()` because it includes two collections. It is built in a `var`, then executed in a separate `await` statement with the `CancellationToken`. The result is named differently from the range variable.

